# <type>(<scope>): <summary>

# Keep the subject at or under 72 characters and drop the trailing period.
# It states the change; the blank line above starts the body, which states why.
# Wrap the body at 100 characters and keep it to 12 lines or fewer.
# If the change is obvious from one line, delete everything below this one.
#
# types:  feat fix docs test refactor perf build ci chore revert style
# scopes: routing host client view schema profile test docs
#
# Leave one blank line before any trailer that git understands
# (Closes #12, Refs: …, Co-authored-by: …).
#
# Attribution lines ("Generated with …", "🤖", AI co-author addresses) are
# rejected: the message describes the change, not the tool that typed it.
#
# Every line above starting with "#" is dropped by git. Set this file as the
# default with:  git config commit.template .gitmessage
